ME:
AI can make decisions for us, but that doesn’t mean we should blindly trust it.
The real question is: when AI acts, are the systems behind it making the right calls? Do we have ways to check, control, and correct if needed?
It’s the infrastructure and oversight behind AI that determines whether it truly works in your best interest.



A payment system can be fast and still create new dependency risks.
The hidden risk is not only payment speed.
The question is:
When your money moves instantly, how confident are you that your bank’s verification and recovery systems are equally fast?

A fintech company’s biggest challenge may not always be its app.
Sometimes, it is the financial infrastructure behind it.


Financial platforms often operate through a combination of:
• Banking relationships
• Payment networks
• Settlement systems
• Regulatory structures

These relationships are usually invisible when everything works normally.




